---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Engineering Notes"
  description="Technical deep-dives into architecture decisions, incident recovery, and systems thinking."
>
  <section class="py-13">
    <nav class="mb-8">
      <a href="/" class="text-14 text-accent no-underline">← Back home</a>
    </nav>

    <h1 class="font-code text-40 font-semibold mb-6">Engineering Notes</h1>

    <p class="text-18 text-ink-2 mb-12 max-w-[65ch]">Deep-dives into decisions, incidents, and lessons from building data platforms and backend infrastructure at scale.</p>

    <!-- Published Notes -->
    <section class="mb-16">
      <h2 class="font-code text-16 font-semibold text-accent uppercase tracking-[0.1em] mb-6">Published</h2>
      <div class="grid gap-6">
        <div class="p-5 bg-panel border border-rule rounded">
          <a href="/engineering-notes/debezium-50m-row-snapshot/" class="no-underline text-inherit">
            <h3 class="text-18 font-semibold text-ink mb-2">The 50M-row Debezium snapshot incident</h3>
            <p class="text-14 text-ink-2">A snapshot operation consumed 60% CPU and nearly blocked a critical migration. How we recovered and what it taught about production risk vs architectural purity.</p>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="pt-2">
      <h2 class="font-code text-16 font-semibold text-accent uppercase tracking-[0.1em] mb-4">Incident record</h2>
      <p class="text-16 text-ink-2 max-w-[65ch] mb-4">Ten production problems covering diagnosis, architecture, customer judgment, correctness, resilience, and leadership under pressure.</p>
      <a href="/engineering-notes/incidents/" class="text-accent font-mono text-14">Read all ten incident records →</a>
    </section>

  </section>
</Layout>
